 #:seon.task{:name "a-core-test-in-a-namespace-the-loaded-program-lacks-is-refused-as-host-bound"
             :kind :function
             :intent "seon.test/run of a :core-admitted test whose namespace this JVM never loaded and the loaded program does not contain (a file analyzed into a branch from outside the classpath, as test/seon/cluster/branch_evidence_test.clj first did) refuses 'Host-bound declaration <ns>/callee must change through the loaded source files.': arm-first-loads! compares the branch's contracts with the loaded program's, and every contract of a namespace absent from the loaded program reads as changed. Nothing there is host-bound; the namespace is unloadable. Done when that request refuses by name as a namespace this JVM cannot load (the message seon.sci.eval uses for unloaded rows), and a regression asserts the refusal's :seon.error/type or member."
             :must-read #{seon.test/run}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-check-compares-every-definition-digest-of-the-program-twice"
             :kind :function
             :intent "One check with no named change runs `seon.test/digest-differences` twice (in `seon.test/changes` and again in `seon.test/program-overlay-tx` under `seon.test/clean-request-handle`): each queries every :seon.program/definition-digest of the published base and of the candidate (about 12,000 rows each) and decodes the result, 41-54 ms per check on a throwaway root (lane check-cost, 2026-10-08), although the base is one immutable commit and the candidate differs from it by the agent's few rows. The same check also derives three whole-program projection content keys (`seon.db/declaration-content-key`, 66-90 ms): the as-of view `seon.test/changed-definition-symbols` reads and the request world's first writes. Done when one check computes the differences once, the base side is cached by its commit, and a one-definition check's difference and projection-key cost is proportional to the change, with a regression counting `seon.test/digest-differences` and `seon.db/declaration-content-key` calls through `seon.mcp/call`."
             :must-read #{seon.test/digest-differences seon.test/changes seon.test/program-overlay-tx seon.test/changed-definition-symbols}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-repl-test-after-a-root-ns-form-has-no-executable-var"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Root evaluated on main the file's (ns seon.ref-test ...) with two added requires, then the deftest seon.ref-test/a-resolved-function-offers-a-source-form-that-shows-its-source (fanout-2 run, default 795a770c2, 2026-10-08). Called at root's or the agent's REPL it runs, but every test-world run of it, on main and on agent fan2-source's branch after a correct fix, records error 1 with began? false and the failure \"The admitted identity has no executable test Var.\", so its task can never go green. Deftests defined the same way in seon.db-test and seon.transact-feedback-test without an ns form run and fail on their assertions. Without an ns form it happens too when the body names the test file's private helpers or aliases (fanout-3, default 324461975, 2026-10-09: root's seon.help-test/help-teaches-how-a-deftest-names-its-task over with-help-agent, taught-forms and the bootstrap alias recorded the same error; the same deftest with only fully qualified calls ran and failed on its assertion), because root's SCI context has not loaded the test namespace. A redefinition at root of a file-derived deftest with only fully qualified calls also loses it on branches (fanout-4, default 97f2b2ac3, 2026-10-09): root re-evaluated seon.db-test/a-missing-connection-refusal-carries-its-fix-as-data and seon.transact-feedback-test/uninstalled-attribute-candidates-are-the-nearest-names after in-ns; on main both ran and failed on their assertions, but on agents fan4-fix and fan4-near's branches every run recorded \"The admitted identity has no executable test Var.\", so two correct fixes never went green there, while a new deftest root defined the same way (seon.error-test/a-missing-name-with-no-near-names-has-no-namespace-list) ran and went green on agent fan4-empty's branch. Done when a deftest root defines at its REPL after an ns form runs in the test world as at the REPL. Also a `def` in a test namespace: a deftest that references a value made by a REPL `def` in its namespace is not run (lane loop-prove, 86b7cdbbe, 2026-10-10): its check answers \"The admitted identity has no executable test Var.\" and leaves a recurring acquisition-refusal error on every later request. A `def` is not program, so the test's reached definitions do not carry it. Done when such a test either runs with the def available in the context or is refused once, at the form that defines it, naming the def and the fix, with no recurring error."
             :must-read #{seon.test/resolve-test seon.test/run}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-proof-that-evaluates-agent-code-reuses-its-red"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Since `f5e4ec35d` (F11, an unchanged red answered from its record) a task proof that reaches the agent's definitions only through evaluated code, as every `seon.competency-test` proof does through `seon.test-support/agent-value`, keeps its first red: its reach digest does not change when the agent defines `comp.geo/area`, so the step answers the old red and the task never goes green. `seon.competency-grade-test/a-fixture-model-run-grades-green` passes at `100f08747` (`bin/seon check --at 100f08747`, run 1078ca606457) and fails at `f5e4ec35d` (run da39358e68af: proofs {:red 1} after the correct model reply), as does `seon.competency-grade-test/a-launch-grades-each-run`. Done when a task's proofs run again after any eval request that changed the branch's program, while unrelated unchanged reds stay answered from their record."
             :must-read #{seon.test/run seon.turn/run-proofs seon.test-support/agent-value}}
 #:seon.task{:name "destructive-reach-keeps-a-second-cache"
             :kind :function
             :intent "seon.test/destructive-reach memoizes its walk in a clojure.core.cache LRU (threshold 4) held in the schema projection's cache value, beside seon.cache: a second cache with its own bound and no recordStats, which AGENTS.md refuses. Done when the walk is a seon.cache kind keyed by the same content key and clojure.core.cache.wrapped is no longer required by seon.test."
             :must-read #{seon.test/destructive-reach seon.cache/lookup}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-malformed-task-tag-stops-the-whole-check"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A malformed `:seon/tasks` value on one deftest stopped a whole `bin/seon check` with an exception (lane h1-prose, 2026-10-09) instead of returning an error on that one test beside the others' results (AGENTS.md: nothing crashes; errors are data)."
             :must-read #{seon.test/run}}
 #:seon.task{:name "changed-definition-symbols-scans-whole-attributes-since-the-last-run"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.test/changed-definition-symbols` reads the changes since the previous run through `seon.db/since` over history, whose attribute-bound clauses still walk each attribute's whole index filtered by transaction, plus two as-of `seon.test/definition-digests` reads: 123-160 ms of every automatic test step on default `dc79b069f` (agent step-growth-1, one defn and one deftest per request), proportional to the program, not to the request's one or two changed rows. Done when the identities changed since a run come from the transactions written since it (the branch commits after the run's basis, or the recording transaction's report the step holds), at a cost proportional to those datoms, with a regression counting reads through `seon.profile/measure`."
             :must-read #{seon.test/changed-definition-symbols seon.test/select seon.db/since}}
 #:seon.task{:name "reach-attribute-advances-from-the-recording-report"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.test.runner/reach-attribute` derives a whole attribute map (about 66 ms to read the eleven reach attributes' 188,000 datoms on default) for every new content revision a branch writes; `seon.test.runner/retire-replaced-revision!` bounds the retained maps to one per branch and attribute, but each eval request still re-reads and rebuilds the attributes it wrote. Done when the test step is handed the eval request's recording transaction report and advances the previous revision's map by its `:tx-data` only when the cached revision equals the report's `:db-before` revision of that attribute (cost-design D1's contiguity check), deriving otherwise, with a regression showing a one-defn request's reach acquisition reads only the datoms it wrote."
             :must-read #{seon.test.runner/reach-attribute seon.turn/test-step seon.db/content-revisions}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/cost-design/merged.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-sci-deftest-with-tasks-reports-no-executable-test-var"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Lane ns-form (agent ns-form, default 7f1e250c6, 2026-10-09) evaluated in seon.program-test a deftest carrying ^{:seon/tasks #{'seon.turn.batch/a-repl-require-changes-the-namespace-context-but-not-its-source}} before its name; (resolve ...) answers the Var with :test metadata and clojure.test/test-var runs it, yet (my.test/check {:seon.test/changed [that symbol]}) answers one error, :seon.test/unchanged true, message \"The admitted identity has no executable test Var.\", and the render's :seon.render.test/failures entry carries only the symbol, not that message. Done when check runs the Var the context holds and a failure entry shows its message."
             :must-read #{seon.test/run}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-first-deftest-in-a-new-namespace-costs-seconds-of-test-step"
             :kind :function
             :intent "On an agent branch (default 6e9b9017c, fan-out 6, agent fan6-key), one eval request `(ns fan6.probe-test (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is]]))` plus one deftest calling `seon.error/explain-problem` cost 3,688 ms, of which the test step 3,525 ms, 798,415 armed calls and 8,080 reads; a redefinition of `seon.error/explain-problem` on a fresh branch cost a 2,054 ms test step plus 462 ms apply. The test itself runs in milliseconds. Done when the step for one new test and its reaching proofs costs about the tests' own run, with a `seon.profile/measure` regression."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/run-reaching seon.test/run-request}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-named-check-drops-declared-long-tests-without-saying-so"
             :kind :function
             :intent "At root on default c7a7030d8 (2026-10-09, fresh reset), `(my.test/check {:seon.test/changed [ten test symbols]})` ran 5 and answered `:seon.test/passed? false` with 5 results and no key naming the other 5 (`seon.cluster.evaluate-source-test/code-evaluates-as-one-ordinary-run-of-its-agent`, `seon.cluster.agent-test/disarm-interrupts-an-in-flight-turn-and-records-it-interrupted`, `seon.cluster.turn-test/a-model-request-is-help-own-exchanges-and-the-block-last`, `seon.sci.context-reads-test/a-branch-redefinition-of-a-loaded-test-runs-under-its-own-bound`, `seon.repl-differential-test/a-file-proof-aliasing-its-subject-runs-green-on-the-branch`), all declared `:seon.test/long`. `my.test/check` already lists `:seon.test/long-excluded` as an answer key, but none was set. Done when a named check answers every named test it did not run under the key saying why, by name."
             :must-read #{my.test/check seon.test/run}}
 #:seon.task{:name "one-test-run-at-the-repl-allocates-over-a-gigabyte"
             :kind :function
             :intent "One small deftest run at an agent's REPL costs about 1.4 s and 0.5 to 1.25 GB. Agent sci-tests on default 18919b663, 2026-10-10: `(clojure.test/run-test-var #'seon.id-test/a-host-object-has-no-identity)` took 444 ms of evaluation and allocated 515 MB, in a 936 ms request with 622 ms of GC. `(seon.profile/measure (fn [] (my.test/check {:seon.test/changed ['seon.id-test/a-host-object-has-no-identity]})))` measured 1,412 ms, 1,248 MB allocated on the thread and 128,464 armed calls. By self time: `seon.db/vector-query-call` 448 ms over 238 calls, `seon.db/transact-call` 360 ms over 8 calls, `seon.db/declaration-content-key` 79 ms over 5 calls and `seon.test/arm-first-loads!` 72 ms. By call count, `seon.sci.eval/copy-host-var` ran 7,460 times and `seon.sci.kernel/mark-installed!` 4,335 times, so the member context re-copies the whole compiled program. The owner is unconfirmed: either the member context acquisition (`seon.cluster.agent/acquire-context!`, `seon.sci.eval/acquire-program!`) or the selection and recording reads in `seon.test/run`. The work should be proportional to one test and its reach, not to the program. Done when the same measure answers under 100 MB and under 200 ms, with a measured-cost proof on the owner."
             :must-read #{my.test/check seon.test/run seon.cluster.agent/acquire-context! seon.sci.eval/acquire-program! seon.sci.eval/copy-host-var seon.db/vector-query-call seon.profile/measure}}
 #:seon.task{:name "select-names-a-changed-test-as-a-function"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.test/select` refuses a changed identity it cannot find with `:seon.test/identity-unresolved` and offending `[:seon.fn/sym value]` whatever the change's attribute: lane merge-path (check run 0e1ca59bb5ea, 2026-10-10) saw a proof passed as `[:seon.test/sym wbfix150a6f88c052.core/caller-check]` reported as `[:seon.fn/sym wbfix150a6f88c052.core/caller-check]`, which reads as a missing function rather than a missing test. Done when the refusal names the change as given, as a row in an existing selection test."
             :must-read #{seon.test/select}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-named-check-on-a-branch-carrying-platform-edits-allocates-gigabytes"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Agent eval-fixes on default 9a23b8ff2 (2026-10-10), its branch carrying the edit hook's interpreted copies of `seon.sci.eval` and `seon.test`: `(my.test/check {:seon.test/identities <17 tests>})` took 18,045 ms and allocated 17,731 MB, executing 76 tests (the 17 named plus the step's reaching tests), with GC 12.4 s in the window. The same 17 named tests on a fresh agent took 7,735 ms and 1,157 MB (run f11a3891e603). Every later evaluation on that branch, a contract refusal included, paid a 10 to 18 s test step. Done when an evaluation that changed no definition runs no reaching test, and a named check's cost is proportional to the named tests."
             :must-read #{my.test/check seon.test/run seon.test/reaching}}
]
